From 0834b34cf0d23699543b5ecb179b06c8303a12bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Dolbeau <romain@dolbeau.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:46:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] m68k: extended precision soft-float routines from soft-fp

libgcc's m68k XFmode routines (fpgnulib.c built with EXTFLOAT) work in
double precision: every operand is converted to DFmode and back, and even
the comparisons compare doubles.  A soft-float program whose long double
is the 80-bit extended format gets 53-bit results where it expects 64,
and wrong decimal conversions in a C library that relies on long double
being exact.  musl's printf, for one, prints 2/3 as 0.666666, 1e100 as
9.99999e+99 and 0.1 as 0.099999999999994316 on such a system (its m68k
soft-float ABI, ld-musl-m68k-sf.so.1).

Use soft-fp instead, in the m68k extended format:

- extended-m68k.h is that format for soft-fp.  It differs from
  soft-fp/extended.h's x87 one at the bottom of the range: an exponent
  of 0 with the explicit integer bit set is a normal number, 2**-16383,
  and a denormal is 0.F * 2**-16383.  So soft-fp works in a format "M"
  with a 16-bit exponent biased by 16384, in which every m68k value is
  exact with soft-fp's own denormal rule, and packing maps back to the 15
  bits, an exponent beyond them overflowing to infinity.  Unnormal
  operands are normalized on the way in, as the MC68881 does.
- The words are 64 bits wide: with 32-bit words the working fraction (67
  bits) does not reach the top of its four words, and soft-fp's addition
  clears the bits a borrow leaves above the fraction only in the word
  holding the implicit bit.
- The functions are soft-fp's TFmode ones in that format: add, sub, mul,
  div, neg, the comparisons, unord, the conversions from and to SFmode,
  DFmode and SImode.  __cmpxf2, which fpgnulib.c also provided, is an
  alias of __lexf2.  NaNs follow the MC68881: its default NaN (positive,
  all fraction bits set) and, between two NaN operands, the first.
- fpgnulib.c keeps its SFmode and DFmode part only.

Tested on the host against x87 long double (98 million results where
the formats agree), and against an exact rational reference where they
do not (m68k's lowest binade, denormals, unnormals); on a 68030 without
FPU, musl's printf now prints what glibc does.

libgcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/m68k/sfp-machine.h: New file.
	* config/m68k/extended-m68k.h: New file.
	* config/m68k/addxf3.c, config/m68k/subxf3.c,
	config/m68k/mulxf3.c, config/m68k/divxf3.c,
	config/m68k/negxf2.c, config/m68k/eqxf2.c,
	config/m68k/gexf2.c, config/m68k/lexf2.c,
	config/m68k/unordxf2.c, config/m68k/extendsfxf2.c,
	config/m68k/extenddfxf2.c, config/m68k/truncxfsf2.c,
	config/m68k/truncxfdf2.c, config/m68k/fixxfsi.c,
	config/m68k/floatsixf.c, config/m68k/floatunsixf.c: New files.
	* config/m68k/t-floatlib (LIB2ADD): Add them instead of
	xfgnulib.c.
	(xfgnulib.c): Remove.
	* config/m68k/fpgnulib.c: Remove the EXTFLOAT part.
